        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "jRZz3",
          "name": "cmp/KanbanRendererCard",
          "context": "The unit of the kanban display. Same resource as cmp/CollectionListRow, drawn as a draggable card instead of a row. radius 6, bg on a border hairline so it lifts off the column's bg.subtle. Top: mono id + spacer + assignee. Title 12/1.35 wraps to two lines. Meta carries the same attribute chips the list shows as columns — the board hides no data, it re-lays it out. Drag target styling is the accent border, not a shadow.\n\nNo state ring: the card sits in a column, and the column header already names and colours the state. Repeating it on every card restates the column ten times over. This holds while the board groups by status — group by something else (assignee, priority) and the state has no other carrier here, so the ring has to come back onto the card.",
          "reusable": true,
          "width": 240,
          "fill": "$ds-bg",
          "cornerRadius": 6,
          "stroke": "$ds-border",
          "strokeWidth": 1,
          "strokeAlignment": "inner",
          "layout": "vertical",
