        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "DuUAX",
          "name": "cmp/KanbanRendererViewBar",
          "context": "The renderer header is transparent and has a fixed 40px saved-view bar plus a conditional 36px filters row. The top bar holds saved views as tabs, New view, and icon-only Filter and Display controls. Filter and Display expose matching hover/focus tooltips, and both use the compact 2xs control size. Each popover opens 8px below its own trigger and right-aligns to that trigger; neither surface is positioned from the viewport edge. The Filter control uses the subtle active surface whenever filters are applied; it never carries a numeric badge.\n\nThe Filters row appears whenever the active view has applied filters, including after those filters are saved. Each clause stays visible as a filter pill so the narrowed dataset is never hidden. If the view is dirty, Reset and Save appear at the right and the active tab carries the warning dot. Display-only edits can also raise the row for those actions even when there are no filter pills.\n\nThe header bottom divider uses $ds-border-subtle. Tabs, buttons, and pills share the compact baseline.",
