        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "IZ2hX",
          "name": "cmp/FilterPill",
          "context": "A committed filter clause. Reads 'Key op Value' then a remove affordance. h 24, radius 4, surface on a border hairline. Key/op are fg.muted, Value is fg at 500 so the clause scans as one phrase with the value emphasised. The x removes the clause, which detaches the active view and raises Save.\n\nAppears in two places: listed inside the Filter modal, and — while the view is being edited — in cmp/ViewBar's Filters subheader. At rest the clauses stay in the modal so the header keeps a fixed height.",
